  "question": {
    "text": "A wire having tension&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>225</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> produces six beats per second when it vibrates with some tuning fork. When the tension changes to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>256</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, it vibrates with the same fork with the number of beats remaining unchanged. The frequency of the fork will be"
